-- title:
--   Level automorphisms transport node place-sets and Igusa ends
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q\ge 5$, $M'$ is a positive integer with $q\nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ for which $q$ is a non-unit ($A.\mathrm{LiesOverPrime}\ q$); $\kappa_A$ denotes the residue field of $A$. The finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A,M')$ is required by `hW` to consist exactly of the supersingular places, i.e. of those places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and whose value $w(\,j\,)$ at the generator `jGeomGen` lies in the supersingular $j$-set for $q$. The field `fieldBar q M'` is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the function field of the curve $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, where $H=\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^{2}M')^{\times}\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^{\times}$, that is, the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$; `hle` asserts that the base change $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot\mathcal F_{M'}$ of the full modular function field of level $M'$ lies inside it. Further, $R_0$ is a constant reduction of $A$ from $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot\mathcal F_{M'}$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A,M')$: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the source agreeing with $A$ on constants, a surjective residue homomorphism to the target with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A\to\kappa_A$, together with a map on places preserving degrees and computing orders. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot\mathcal F_{M'}$ belongs to `R₀.integers` and that its residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa_A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $s\in W$ is a chosen supersingular place.
--
--   The arithmetic base data are: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ with $\pi_0\in A$, such that $A_0:=A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hdvr`, `hunif`), is Henselian (`hhens`), has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and such that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$ (`hκ`); an auxiliary prime $\ell$ with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and an element $\varpi_t\in k_0\cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^{2}-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$; a family $K:\iota\to$ intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$, each finite over $k_0$, with valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K_n$ cut out by $A$ (`hAn`), a least index $n_0$ ($K_{n_0}\le K_n$ for all $n$) and the cofinality condition `hKcof` that every finite subset of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is contained in some $K_n$; an element $\pi_t\in A$ with $\pi_t^{q^{2}-1}=q$ and the tameness condition `htame` that every element of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ on which the tame character attached to $\pi_t$ is trivial fixes $K_{n_0}$ pointwise; and the bottom layer $K_b=\bot$ with its valuation subring $A_b$ cut out by $A$ and a generator $\varpi_b\ne 0$ of its maximal ideal.
--
--   The assertion is a universally quantified implication. It ranges over all intermediate fields $F_0$ of $(\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M')/k_0$ satisfying four conditions: $F_0$ consists exactly of the elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $k_0$; the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the constants $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is everything; $F_0$ is stable under every level automorphism $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $\zeta\in\mathrm{Idx}\,q$ (a primitive $q$-th root of unity) and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; and a linear disjointness clause: for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, any $K'$-linearly independent family $c_1,\dots,c_m\in\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and any $a_1,\dots,a_m$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ forces all $a_i=0$.
--
--   It then ranges over a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$, a subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with an $A_b$-algebra structure, witnesses that the base-changed $q$-expansion $j_q$ lies in `R₀.integers` (`hjR`) and that its residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$ (`hjs`), a witness `hJK` that $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,q$ lies in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, an element $a_0\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue satisfies $\overline{a_0}^{\,q}=s(\overline{j})$ (`hpin`), and a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$.
--
--   The hypothesis imposed on this data is one long conjunction, whose groups are summarised here. (i) *Constants and uniformiser for $W_0$*: $W_0$ cuts out $A$ on $k_0$, is a discrete valuation ring, and has maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$. (ii) *Reduction at $s$*: for every $g$ in the full modular function field of level $M'$ whose base change lies in `R₀.integers` and which has non-negative order at every place at which $j_q$ has non-negative order, if the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$ then the image of $g$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue equals the value at $s$ of that residue, the image of $g$ minus $c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$. (iii) *Level invariance of $W_0$*: for $\zeta$, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $f\in F_0$ with $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,f\in F_0$, membership of $f$ in $W_0$ is equivalent to membership of its image. (iv) *The model $B$*: the $A_b$-algebra structure is the one induced by $A_b\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; $B$ lies in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by $K_b$, and every element of that compositum is a ratio of two elements of $B$; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$ and $B/(\varpi_b)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; $B\subseteq F_0$ with all its elements in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ is prime in $B$ and $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ away from it; $j_q$ lies in $B$ and $B$ is stable under all level automorphisms; there is an element of $B\cap F_0$ lying outside every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ that cuts out $A$ on $k_0$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains $j_q$ and makes every monic polynomial with coefficients in $k_0\cap A$ evaluated at $j_q$ a unit of $V$; for each supersingular place $s'\in W$ with $s'\ne s$ there is an element of $B\cap F_0$ lying outside every valuation subring of $F_0$ that cuts out $A$ on $k_0$ and satisfies the analogue of (ii) at $s'$; and for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^{2}}$-algebra structure on $\kappa_A$ making $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa_A$ a domain and every $\zeta$, there are a subgroup $C$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb{F}_{q^{2}}$ with $\#C=2\cdot\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to the $C$-fixed field of the Drinfeld function field over $\kappa_A$, with kernel $(\varpi_b)$, compatible with $A_b\to\kappa_A$, whose image has the fixed field as field of fractions and consists exactly of the elements lying in the image of $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa_A$, and which intertwines the level automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}$ for those $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ in $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$ with the action $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}$. (v) *The node presentation*: `nodes` has $q+1$ elements; there is a subring $B_c$ of $F_0$, generated by the constants in $k_0\cap A$ together with a finite set, contained in every $O\in$ `nodes` and with each such $O$ its localisation; the level automorphisms permute `nodes` and act transitively on it; distinct nodes are separated by an element that is a non-unit in one and a unit in the other; every valuation subring of $F_0$ cutting out $A$ on $k_0$ and satisfying (ii) either contains $B$ or dominates some node; and each $O\in$ `nodes` is contained in $W_0$, is local and Noetherian, cuts out $A$ on $k_0$, has every element congruent to a constant modulo its non-units, and carries a crossing datum: an exponent $E_0\ge 1$ together with a unit $v$ of $A$ in $k_0$ with $\pi_0^{E_0}=\varpi_t^{\,2\cdot\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s}v$, elements $c_x,c_y\in O$ and a unit $u$ with $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$, an isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion of $O$ with the crossing model $\widehat{A_0}[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-\pi_0^{E_0})$ carrying constants to constants and $c_x,c_y$ to unit multiples of the two distinguished elements `UVCrossingModel.U` and `UVCrossingModel.V`, with $c_y$ in the maximal ideal of $W_0$ and $c_x$ a unit there; an Igusa clause stating that $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,q-a_0$ lies in $F_0$ and in $O$ and that $\iota$ carries it to a unit times the $e$-th power of `UVCrossingModel.V` for some $e\ge 1$; a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ containing $O$, cutting out $A$ on $k_0$, discrete with uniformiser $\pi_0$, carrying an element at which no polynomial with coefficients in $k_0\cap A$ can take a value in the maximal ideal unless all its coefficients do, with $c_x$ in and $c_y$ outside its maximal ideal, computing the $R_0$-residues of modular functions as in (ii) (membership in the maximal ideal being equivalent to vanishing of the residue, and the $s$-integral ones landing in $O$ congruent to the corresponding constant), and excluding every other node; and a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ contained in $B\cap O$, whose elements are regular wherever $j_q$ is, with $O$ its localisation, with $F_0$ its field of fractions, generated by the constants in $k_0\cap A$ and a finite set, and containing an element excluded by every valuation subring as in (iv) that fails to contain all of $O$.
--
--   Under all of this, the conclusion is again universally quantified. It ranges over a field $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa_A$ and a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ to $F_{ss}$ (a valuation subring with surjective residue map onto $F_{ss}$, kernel its maximal ideal, agreeing with $A$ on constants) whose integers trace $W_0$ on $F_0$; over a finite set $N$ of places of $F_{ss}$ and a map `Oof` from places to subrings of $F_0$ restricting to a bijection from $N$ onto `nodes`; over a map $S$ assigning to each place of $F_{ss}$ a set of places of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that for $nd\in N$ the set $S(nd)$ consists exactly of the places $P$ dominating the node $\mathrm{Oof}(nd)$, i.e. containing it in their valuation subring and sending its non-units into the maximal ideal of $A$ under $P$-evaluation; subject to the centre condition that for each $nd\in N$ the $R$-residues of the elements of $\mathrm{Oof}(nd)$ lie in the valuation subring of $nd$, the residues of its non-units lie in the maximal ideal of $nd$, and $nd$ is the unique place of $F_{ss}$ with these two properties; and over families $F_{I,x}$ of fields over $\kappa_A$, regular prolongations $R_x$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ to $F_{I,x}$ and valuation subrings $W_x$ of $F_0$ such that, for $nd\in N$, $R_x(nd)$ traces $W_x(nd)$ on $F_0$, $\mathrm{Oof}(nd)\subseteq W_x(nd)$, $\pi_0$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x(nd)$, and there is an element $c_{y,O}$ of $\mathrm{Oof}(nd)$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_x(nd)$ whose $R$-residue is $0$ and such that every valuation subring of $F_0$ containing $\mathrm{Oof}(nd)$, with $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal and $c_{y,O}$ outside it, contains $W_x(nd)$.
--
--   The assertion for this data is the conjunction of two equivariance statements.
--
--   First: for every $\zeta'\in\mathrm{Idx}\,q$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ there is a self-map $\tau_N$ of the places of $F_{ss}$ such that for every $nd\in N$ one has $\tau_N(nd)\in N$; for every place $P$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $(\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma)\cdot P\in S(nd)$ holds if and only if $P\in S(\tau_N(nd))$; and the preimage of the integers of $R_x(nd)$ under the ring homomorphism underlying $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ is the integers of $R_x(\tau_N(nd))$.
--
--   Second: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}(\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M')$ generated by the level automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, and for every witness that $\tau$ preserves the integers of $R$ (that is, $\tau f$ lies in `R.integers` exactly when $f$ does), and for every $nd\in N$: the place $(\mathrm{R.resAut}\,\tau)\cdot nd$, obtained by acting with the automorphism of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa_A$ induced by $\tau$ on residues, again lies in $N$, and the translate $\mathrm{smulDisc}\,\tau\,(S(nd))=\{P:\tau^{-1}\cdot P\in S(nd)\}$ equals $S\bigl((\mathrm{R.resAut}\,\tau)\cdot nd\bigr)$.
--
--   This is the equivariance half of the per-node analysis of the semistable fibre at $q$ of the modular curve of level $q^{2}M'$ with units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$: granted a presentation of the $q+1$ node rings over a supersingular point $s$, together with their dominating place-sets and their Igusa-side regular prolongations, the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$ permute these data compatibly. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodeCore_nodeCharts_hasseGerm_nodeCentre_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodeCore_nodeCharts_hasseGerm_nodeCentre_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep), where the node core of the layered node presentation is assembled.
